(5157539, 748066, 24486, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NstiG8tr:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ja-9:</b></div><hr/><i> bow should have been bigger...don''t really like these kind of pictures...sorry  a little to much in my face...but your photo is clean and crisp </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ya know if a person don''t like this type of photo why wouldn''t they just pass it by and not even vote or comment on it instead of letting everybody know they don''t like it.<br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Your kidding, right? We all wonder why someone gives us an anonomous less than favourable vote &amp; doesn''t tell us why. When someone comes along &amp; expresses what they truely think, it should be encouraged not knocked back. If we only ever get good comments, we will never grow. <br/> <br/>Congratulations on the blue ribbon.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by NstiG8tr: Originally posted by Ja-9: bow should have been bigger...don''t really like these kind of pictures...sorry  a little to much in my face...but your photo is clean and crisp   Ya know if a person don''t like this type of photo why wouldn''t they just pass it by and not even vote or comment on it instead of letting everybody know they don''t like it.  Your kidding, right? We all wonder why someone gives us an anonomous less than favourable vote & doesn''t tell us why. When someone comes along & expresses what they truely think, it should be encouraged not knocked back. If we only ever get good comments, we will never grow.  Congratulations on the blue ribbon.', '2008-12-30 05:04:48.000000', NULL, 0),
