(5161419, 748101, 54645, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Initial feeling: Sweet, gentle shot of Eeyore, Piglet considering some mischief. I like the feeling, but the angled line of the corner, the blue clips, along with the constant search for what they are waiting for, is distracting.<br/> <br/>Composition: Not bad, I like it with one exception. As a suggestion, cropping out the right blurred third would help.<br/> <br/>Color: The selective desat helps to bring out yous subjects, but the blue on the wall is very destracting. Also, I would suggest bumping the brightness to bring out the colors of the bed and animals.<br/> <br/>I like the idea, and I believe I understand what, and who, they are waiting for!<br/> <br/>Keep shooting. Cheers! Ben</td>', 'Critique Club Initial feeling: Sweet, gentle shot of Eeyore, Piglet considering some mischief. I like the feeling, but the angled line of the corner, the blue clips, along with the constant search for what they are waiting for, is distracting. Composition: Not bad, I like it with one exception. As a suggestion, cropping out the right blurred third would help. Color: The selective desat helps to bring out yous subjects, but the blue on the wall is very destracting. Also, I would suggest bumping the brightness to bring out the colors of the bed and animals. I like the idea, and I believe I understand what, and who, they are waiting for! Keep shooting. Cheers! Ben', '2008-12-31 23:39:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(5161726, 749092, 56417, '<td valign="top">hey, being a Nikon man, I''m on your side....but since this was an advanced editing, it may have helped to selectively dodge parts of this to make it look more 3d... and it could use a little sharpening...; )   but overall a nice shot</td>', 'hey, being a Nikon man, I''m on your side....but since this was an advanced editing, it may have helped to selectively dodge parts of this to make it look more 3d... and it could use a little sharpening...; )   but overall a nice shot', '2009-01-01 01:19:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5161900, 749120, 63633, '<td valign="top">I think this was under-rated Enzo (I gave it a 7), but I find the slightly soft focus on parts of the face distracting. I''m sure it would have scored better if you had taken a few separate shots with different points of focus and combined them in post to increase the DOF on the face of the watch (like Scarbrd did on image <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=717194" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/914/120/717194.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/914/120/717194.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/914/120/717194.jpg"/></a>).</td>', 'I think this was under-rated Enzo (I gave it a 7), but I find the slightly soft focus on parts of the face distracting. I''m sure it would have scored better if you had taken a few separate shots with different points of focus and combined them in post to increase the DOF on the face of the watch (like Scarbrd did on image ).', '2009-01-01 05:16:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(5161982, 748066, 16230, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NstiG8tr:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by 3DsArcher:</b></div><hr/><i> Your kidding, right? We all wonder why someone gives us an anonomous less than favourable vote &amp; doesn''t tell us why. When someone comes along &amp; expresses what they truely think, it should be encouraged not knocked back. If we only ever get good comments, we will never grow. <br/> <br/>Congratulations on the blue ribbon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>No! I''m not kidding! There''s nothing complimenting the photo except saying it''s clean and crisp. The rest is just an expression of someones dislike of the content. I personally don''t consider that to be constructive critisism. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Where is it written that all comments must be compliments? I''m not aware of any such rule. Ja-9 has a right to her opinion just like everyone else here.<br/> <br/>I don''t much care for this photo either. I love good nude photos, but I think they should be sexy and this just doesn''t cut it. The model looks nervous and stiff and the pose is rather awkward.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by NstiG8tr: Originally posted by 3DsArcher: Your kidding, right? We all wonder why someone gives us an anonomous less than favourable vote & doesn''t tell us why. When someone comes along & expresses what they truely think, it should be encouraged not knocked back. If we only ever get good comments, we will never grow.  Congratulations on the blue ribbon.   No! I''m not kidding! There''s nothing complimenting the photo except saying it''s clean and crisp. The rest is just an expression of someones dislike of the content. I personally don''t consider that to be constructive critisism.  Where is it written that all comments must be compliments? I''m not aware of any such rule. Ja-9 has a right to her opinion just like everyone else here. I don''t much care for this photo either. I love good nude photos, but I think they should be sexy and this just doesn''t cut it. The model looks nervous and stiff and the pose is rather awkward.', '2009-01-01 06:23:38.000000', NULL, 0),
