(5168463, 749083, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b>  Great focus and a I like the fairly deep depth of field.  I also like your choice to use selective desaturation for this one, though I am not normally a selective desat fan.  The red behind the headrest of the chair in the foreground is a bit distracting.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Nicely lit.  I like that the city background is a touch overexposed.  It really helps to keep the eye focused on the subjects.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I''d like to see the entire footrests.  Chopping such a small portion of the chair off seems like more of an accident that intentional composition.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> I took this one as more of an open challenge, so you met the challenge no matter what YOU wanted for Christmas.  I like the image, but I think the composition could have been a bit better.  5.6 is a pretty strong score for the image as it is.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical:  Great focus and a I like the fairly deep depth of field.  I also like your choice to use selective desaturation for this one, though I am not normally a selective desat fan.  The red behind the headrest of the chair in the foreground is a bit distracting. Lighting: Nicely lit.  I like that the city background is a touch overexposed.  It really helps to keep the eye focused on the subjects. Composition/Content: I''d like to see the entire footrests.  Chopping such a small portion of the chair off seems like more of an accident that intentional composition. My Opinion: I took this one as more of an open challenge, so you met the challenge no matter what YOU wanted for Christmas.  I like the image, but I think the composition could have been a bit better.  5.6 is a pretty strong score for the image as it is. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2009-01-03 20:04:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5168508, 748066, 70896, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NstiG8tr:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ja-9:</b></div><hr/><i> bow should have been bigger...don''t really like these kind of pictures...sorry  a little to much in my face...but your photo is clean and crisp </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ya know if a person don''t like this type of photo why wouldn''t they just pass it by and not even vote or comment on it instead of letting everybody know they don''t like it.<br/>Nice capture by the way. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This is exactly the reason I dont come in here that often anymore... if you dont comment they b*tch about it, if you do, they also b*tch about it!!!! The point of this place was to learn... hard to do that with a closed mind... <br/> <br/>About the pic, wouldnt have picked it as a first place, but lighting and detail are beautiful. I agree the model looks a little stiff and nervous. Maybe have her turn her head to the side? I havent seen the out takes (i will in a minute), so disregard if her head is turned in one of them.  In any case, congratulations on your ribbon! <br/> <br/>I''m keeping my fingers crossed nobody will sacrifice me for saying something negative!  (not)</td>', 'Originally posted by NstiG8tr: Originally posted by Ja-9: bow should have been bigger...don''t really like these kind of pictures...sorry  a little to much in my face...but your photo is clean and crisp   Ya know if a person don''t like this type of photo why wouldn''t they just pass it by and not even vote or comment on it instead of letting everybody know they don''t like it.Nice capture by the way.   This is exactly the reason I dont come in here that often anymore... if you dont comment they b*tch about it, if you do, they also b*tch about it!!!! The point of this place was to learn... hard to do that with a closed mind...  About the pic, wouldnt have picked it as a first place, but lighting and detail are beautiful. I agree the model looks a little stiff and nervous. Maybe have her turn her head to the side? I havent seen the out takes (i will in a minute), so disregard if her head is turned in one of them.  In any case, congratulations on your ribbon!  I''m keeping my fingers crossed nobody will sacrifice me for saying something negative!  (not)', '2009-01-03 20:15:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5169195, 748674, 12611, '<td valign="top">You''ve posted a lot of bleak and desolate shots in winter.This one gets movement form the blur and thats very nice. But perhaps it is more aptly titled stopping by woods... a bleak and desolate Frost poem, Still and icy, introspective and pensive.</td>', 'You''ve posted a lot of bleak and desolate shots in winter.This one gets movement form the blur and thats very nice. But perhaps it is more aptly titled stopping by woods... a bleak and desolate Frost poem, Still and icy, introspective and pensive.', '2009-01-04 00:24:50.000000', NULL, 0),
